## 4. Architecture

### 4.1 Conceptual Layers

**Presentation / Client Layer**  
React 18 single-page application running entirely in the user's browser. Responsible for UI rendering, state management (search input, weather data), and direct API consumption.

**Web Server Layer**  
Nginx (high-performance, event-driven web server). Configured as a simple static file server with gzip compression, security headers, and automatic HTTP → HTTPS redirect. Serves pre-built assets from `/var/www/html`.

**Infrastructure Layer (AWS)**  
- Virtual Private Cloud (default VPC)
- EC2 t2.micro instance (Ubuntu 24.04)
- Security Group (stateful firewall): inbound rules for SSH (22), HTTP (80), HTTPS (443)
- Elastic IP (stable public address 15.135.246.56)
- EBS gp3 root volume (persistent storage survives stop/start)

**External Data Layer**  
Public HTTPS APIs (no keys required for basic tier):
- BOM: http://www.bom.gov.au/fwo/... JSON feeds
- Open-Meteo: https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast (BOM model)

