## 7. Challenges Encountered & Solutions (Evidence of Learning)

| Challenge | Root Cause | Solution Applied | Lesson Learned |
|-----------|------------|------------------|---------------|
| EACCES permission denied on `npm install` | Folder owned by root from `sudo git clone` | `sudo chown -R ubuntu:ubuntu "folder"` | Always manage ownership when mixing sudo and user-space tools (npm) |
| `dist/*` not found after clone | `dist/` is in .gitignore (standard for Vite) and was never pushed | Build on the server itself (`npm run build`) | Git should contain source only; build artifacts generated in CI/CD or on server |
| Messy folder structure after initial upload | Manual file upload via GitHub web UI created extra folders | Clean re-clone + careful `cp` of only dist contents | Prefer `git clone` over manual uploads for reproducibility |
| Wrong `cd` command / stuck in `>` prompt | Typo in folder name + unclosed quote | `Ctrl+C` to cancel, then correct quoted path | Careful quoting for paths with spaces; Linux is case-sensitive |
| `sudo` asking for password on fresh instance | AWS Ubuntu default is NOPASSWD, but state can change | `sudo passwd ubuntu` (set temp password) or fix sudoers | Understand sudoers configuration on cloud images |
| 404 errors after deployment | Nginx root pointed to wrong location or dist not copied | Verified paths + `try_files` for SPA | Test thoroughly after every file operation |
| DNS not resolving or showing parking page | Conflicting default records (CNAME/URL redirect) | Deleted parking records; added clean A records only | Always audit existing DNS records before adding new ones |

These challenges were not obstacles but valuable learning experiences that deepened understanding of Linux permissions, DNS, deployment pipelines, and systematic debugging — skills directly transferable to professional cloud/devops/cyber roles.

