### C.1 Weather Data Fetch Function (Client-Side)

```jsx
// src/utils/weatherApi.js
const BASE_URL = 'https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast';

export async function fetchWeatherData(latitude, longitude) {
  try {
    const response = await fetch(
      `${BASE_URL}?latitude=${latitude}&longitude=${longitude}` +
      `&current=temperature_2m,relative_humidity_2m,apparent_temperature,` +
      `precipitation,weather_code,wind_speed_10m&daily=weather_code,` +
      `temperature_2m_max,temperature_2m_min,precipitation_sum&timezone=auto`
    );

    if (!response.ok) {
      throw new Error(`HTTP error! status: ${response.status}`);
    }

    const data = await response.json();
    return data;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error fetching weather data:', error);
    throw error;
  }
}
```

**Explanation:**  
This function uses the native `fetch` API to retrieve current weather and 7-day forecast data from Open-Meteo (which includes the BOM ACCESS-G model for Australia). It is called from React components when a user searches for a location. Error handling is included for robustness.

